hTheWolf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T17:56:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T17:56:19Z","body":"I think I face similar issue in my project, but in my case I am using blend space 1D. Anyway it seems when animations use audio tracks, sometimes, pretty randomly all sounds just dissapear. In my case animations with audio tracks are used by monsters and what I also noticed is that when monster is killed and its object is freed, audio come back (but only then, if object remains all sounds are muted).\n\nI haven't noticed such issues in 4.4.1 though (at least in my project), but when I moved to 4.5 this mute issue happens pretty often.\n\nI also tested that when I disable all audio tracks in animations I wasn't able to reproduce it yet.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315140712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315695284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-3315695284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":3315695284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FoX60","user":{"login":"HakanBacon","id":138242235,"node_id":"U_kgDOCD1ouw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138242235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon","html_url":"https://github.com/HakanBacon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HakanBacon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T08:11:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T08:11:26Z","body":"I have forgotten to mention the fact that calling methods this way is also quite irregular. A function that creates footsteps beneath the Player's feet gets calles whenever the foot touches the ground, but in the video it is also clear that this happens only every now and then. This causes no other issues though and is not game breaking whatsoever.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315695284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315983997","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-3315983997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":3315983997,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FpeZ9","user":{"login":"GlyphTheWolf","id":97635482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdHMmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97635482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf","html_url":"https://github.com/GlyphTheWolf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlyphTheWolf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T13:05:13Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T13:05:13Z","body":"Some additional information from tests I did in my project:\n\n1. I confirmed that when mute issue happens and I disable animation tree of monster all audio come back\n2. Issue also doesn't seems to be reproduced when I disable audio tracks from animations used in blend spaces\n3. Issue seems to be not reproduced even when using blend spaces when I use `AnimationTree` with non-deterministic mode\n\nI hope maybe this will help in fixing this issue or at least may be used as workaround.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315983997/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506460086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-3506460086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":3506460086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RAFW2","user":{"login":"fryingpanjoe","id":997300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/997300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe","html_url":"https://github.com/fryingpanjoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fryingpanjoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-08T11:21:49Z","updated_at":"2025-11-09T15:08:05Z","body":"I've also had this, or a very similar, issue for quite a while (at least since 4.3)! A possible solution is to use Call Method Track instead of Audio Playback Track, but it comes with certain limitations.\n\nIt seems like it goes away if I choose \"Don't Use Blend\" on the Audio Playback Track. This causes sounds not to blend with animations properly so you lose volume scaling etc, which may or may not be fine for you. That said, there's a bug where the \"Don't Use Blend\" property gets reset on reimport. I've reported that issue #112552 along with my attempted fix.\n\nEdit: added clarifications and link to blend issue","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506460086/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4159902371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-4159902371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":4159902371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc738xKj","user":{"login":"Phlegmlee","id":152333980,"node_id":"U_kgDOCRRunA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152333980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee","html_url":"https://github.com/Phlegmlee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T05:02:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T05:42:31Z","body":"Updating this for 4.6, I am also having this issue with any `audio playback track` when using the animation with an `AnimationTree`\n\nUsing @fryingpanjoe's recommendation to set the audio track to no blend does seem to work but the volume scaling is sorely missed.\n\nEDIT: I replaced all `audio playback track`'s with a method call `_play_sfx_test()` and the issue was not present. This also introduces some other issues that would need workarounds, but, it is better than audio completely cutting out.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4159902371/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5407556885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-5407556885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":5407556885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQlDFFQ","user":{"login":"feeib","id":82524202,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTI0MjAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82524202?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib","html_url":"https://github.com/feeib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T08:24:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T08:25:10Z","body":"I also have this problem in version 4.7.2. It works the same way when the game starts, all sounds are fine, but after some time, all audio in the game disappears completely. I tested it on different operating systems and got the same result. \n\nhttps://youtu.be/NtPFZDEDVng\n\nI also started to suspect the audio tracks inside the animations, but I wasn't sure how they could cause this. However, I noticed that turning off \"deterministic\" on the AnimationMixer (AnimationTree) seems to fix the problem for a while, even though it makes the audio mixing a bit worse.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5407556885/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614836694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109119#issuecomment-5614836694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109119","id":5614836694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTqub1g","user":{"login":"Phlegmlee","id":152333980,"node_id":"U_kgDOCRRunA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152333980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee","html_url":"https://github.com/Phlegmlee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phlegmlee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:52Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T07:30:52Z","body":"> I also have this problem in version 4.7.2. It works the same way when the game starts, all sounds are fine, but after some time, all audio in the game disappears completely. I tested it on different operating systems and got the same result. \n\n\nI got around to updating an old project to 4.7, it uses the fix in my previous comment of using a method track in the animation instead of an audio track.\n\nI also updated it to call the `play()` method instead of the weird second hand method I was using. It works without cutting out.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5614836694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]